  "caveats": [
    "1. In H_3(q), standard N=2 Jones and N=3 sl_3 HOMFLY-PT quantum-dimension traces of T(3,5) yield 3-term and 6-term Laurent polynomials and do NOT collapse to (q - q^-1)[10]_q; the clean binomial q^10 - q^-10 arises uniquely from the partition-conjugation antisymmetric (w_3, w_21, w_111) = (1, 0, -1) top-channel difference and from the 5-fold strand-period denominator of the symmetrized Alexander / 3-strand reduced Burau invariant. 2. All 15 pre-registered zero-parameter two-loop Delta_2 candidates (29 signed variants) are reported verbatim without post-hoc selection: 27/29 miss outside 2*sigma_CODATA, while C3c (+hbar_q^2*zeta(3)/pi^2, +0.0994 ppb, 0.65 sigma) and C2d (+Vol(4_1)/(12*pi)^2, +0.1898 ppb, 1.24 sigma) lie within 1 sigma and 2 sigma respectively; because 2*sigma_CODATA/alpha^2 spans ~7.89e-4 around c_2^(+,emp) = +9.40e-4 and every candidate shares the steep tree q-slope (~6.43e6 ppm/q across q_0 +- 0.05), neither C3c nor C2d is promoted to production (Rule 14). 3. On WeakVertexTwoTerm, strand charge assignments (e.g. C-lep) and covariance-group choices enter as explicit hypotheses per owner rulings (#8743, #8838)."
